<title>UK: Energy Group replace Redland in FTSE 100.</title>
<headline>Energy Group replace Redland in FTSE 100.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The FTSE Actuaries UK Indices Committee said on Friday The Energy Group Plc would replace Redland Plc in the FTSE 100 share index following the demerger of Hanson Plc.</p>
<p>The committee said Hanson would remain in the FTSE 100 share index and Redland would join the FTSE 250 Index. In turn, Dorling Kindersley Plc would be removed from the FTSE 250 and placed in the FTSE SmallCap Index.</p>
<p>The committee said Granada Group Plc would replace Hanson in the FT 30 index. The changes will come into effect on Monday.</p>
<p>Shareholders in Hanson today approved the group's demerger, clearing the way for the Energy Group division to be spun off on Monday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
